course: dictionary
lesson: 3751
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues in the sentence tell you which meaning the writer wants. Fluke can mean a lucky chance, a flat worm, a part of a whale's tail, or part of an anchor. Read the words around it first, then choose.
explain: «It was a fluke!» said Sam, when the ball bounced off his foot and into the net. Nobody planned it. A fluke is a lucky chance, something good that happens by accident, not because of skill.
explain: «Whale tails move up and down, while fish tails move side to side, and humpbacks can be recognised by the pattern under their flukes.» The clues are whale, humpbacks and tails. So here flukes means the flat parts of a whale's tail, not luck.
explain: Always check: what does the word mean in this sentence? Put your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense. If it does, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Fluke has more than one meaning, so always check the context.
fact: A fluke can mean a lucky chance, something good that happened by accident.
fact: A fluke can also be a flat parasitic worm that can live inside animals or people.
fact: The flukes are the two flat parts of a whale's tail, and they move up and down.
fact: The fluke is also the flat pointed part of an anchor's arm.
exercise: «It was a fluke!» said Sam when his shot went in off the post. What does fluke mean here? | The pointed arm of an anchor | The tail of a whale | A flat worm living inside a fish | *A lucky chance, not because of skill
exercise: «Its tail flukes beat up and down, not side to side like a fish.» Which part of a whale is a fluke? | A fin on its back | Its eyes | *The two flat parts of its tail | Its mouth
exercise: A scientist gets one odd result in a test and says it was a fluke. What does she probably mean? | It was the best result ever, because of great skill | The test proves she was right forever | *It happened by chance, so she will repeat the test | A worm got into the test tube
test: «The sheep was ill because a flat worm was living inside it.» Which meaning of fluke fits? | A lucky chance | The arm of an anchor | *A flat parasitic worm | The tail of a whale
test: «The boat's anchor had a fluke that caught in the sand.» What is the fluke? | *The flat pointed part of the anchor's arm | Part of a whale's tail | A lucky chance | A flat worm
exam: Jo says, «We won the match by a fluke, not because we played well.» What does Jo mean? | Jo means the team lost on purpose | Jo means the team trained hard for years | Jo means a whale was in the match | *Jo means the win was lucky, not due to skill
